<speak>For a while, yes. Some relationships go back a long way, and I would rather introduce the change in person than announce that somebody else is now responsible. The younger managers know the business very well. What they have not inherited is the history behind certain conversations. A supplier may refer to an old difficulty without explaining it, and I know what they mean. I am trying to put that background into useful notes instead of leaving it all in my head. It is not a matter of telling the managers what to say. It is giving them enough context to speak for themselves.</speak>